msgid "Highlights:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:183
msgid "The asyncio reactor is now enabled by default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:185
msgid ""
"Replaced ``start_requests()`` (sync) with :meth:`~scrapy.Spider.start` "
"(async) and changed how it is iterated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:188
msgid "Added the :reqmeta:`allow_offsite` request meta key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:190
msgid ""
"Spider middlewares that don't support asynchronous spider output are "
"deprecated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:193
msgid ""
"Added a base class for :ref:`universal spider middlewares <universal-spider-"
"middleware>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:199
msgid "Dropped support for PyPy 3.9. (:gh:`6613`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:202
msgid "Added support for PyPy 3.11. (:gh:`6697`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:206 ../../../news/2.x.rst:761
#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1515 ../../../news/2.x.rst:1668
#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:2556 ../../../news/2.x.rst:3183
#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:3584 ../../../news/2.x.rst:3772
#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:3940
msgid "Backward-incompatible changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:208
msgid ""
"The default value of the :setting:`TWISTED_REACTOR` setting was changed from "
"``None`` to ``\"twisted.internet.asyncioreactor.AsyncioSelectorReactor\"``. "
"This value was used in newly generated projects since Scrapy 2.7.0 but now "
"existing projects that don't explicitly set this setting will also use the "
"asyncio reactor. You can :ref:`change this setting in your project <disable-"
"asyncio>` to use a different reactor. (:gh:`6659`, :gh:`6713`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:217
msgid ""
"The iteration of start requests and items no longer stops once there are "
"requests in the scheduler, and instead runs continuously until all start "
"requests have been scheduled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:221
msgid ""
"To reproduce the previous behavior, see :ref:`start-requests-lazy`. (:gh:"
"`6729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:224
msgid ""
"An unhandled exception from the :meth:`~scrapy.spidermiddlewares."
"SpiderMiddleware.open_spider` method of a :ref:`spider middleware <topics-"
"spider-middleware>` no longer stops the crawl. (:gh:`6729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:230
msgid "In ``scrapy.core.engine.ExecutionEngine``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:232
msgid ""
"The second parameter of ``open_spider()``, ``start_requests``, has been "
"removed. The start requests are determined by the ``spider`` parameter "
"instead (see :meth:`~scrapy.Spider.start`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:236
msgid ""
"The ``slot`` attribute has been renamed to ``_slot`` and should not be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:239
msgid "(:gh:`6729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:241
msgid ""
"In ``scrapy.core.engine``, the ``Slot`` class has been renamed to ``_Slot`` "
"and should not be used. (:gh:`6729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:245
msgid ""
"The ``slot`` :ref:`telnet variable <telnet-vars>` has been removed. (:gh:"
"`6729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:248
msgid ""
"In ``scrapy.core.spidermw.SpiderMiddlewareManager``, "
"``process_start_requests()`` has been replaced by ``process_start()``. (:gh:"
"`6729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:252
msgid ""
"The ``scrape_func`` callable passed to ``scrapy.core.spidermw."
"SpiderMiddlewareManager.scrape_response()`` is now called with 2 parameters, "
"``response`` and ``request``, instead of 3, and must return a :class:"
"`~twisted.internet.defer.Deferred` instead of an iterable. (:gh:`6787`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:259
msgid ""
"The now-deprecated ``start_requests()`` method, when it returns an iterable "
"instead of being defined as a generator, is now executed *after* the :ref:"
"`scheduler <topics-scheduler>` instance has been created. (:gh:`6729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:264
msgid ""
"When using :setting:`JOBDIR`, :ref:`start requests <start-requests>` are now "
"serialized into their own, ``s``-suffixed priority folders. You can set :"
"setting:`SCHEDULER_START_DISK_QUEUE` to ``None`` or ``\"\"`` to change that, "
"but the side effects may be undesirable. See :setting:"
"`SCHEDULER_START_DISK_QUEUE` for details. (:gh:`6729`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:271
msgid ""
"The URL length limit, set by the :setting:`URLLENGTH_LIMIT` setting, is now "
"also enforced for start requests. (:gh:`6777`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:275
msgid ""
"Calling ``scrapy.utils.reactor.is_asyncio_reactor_installed`` without an "
"installed reactor now raises an exception instead of installing a reactor. "
"This shouldn't affect normal Scrapy use cases, but it may affect 3rd-party "
"test suites that use Scrapy internals such as :class:`~scrapy.crawler."
"Crawler` and don't install a reactor explicitly. If you are affected by this "
"change, you most likely need to install the reactor before running Scrapy "
"code that expects it to be installed. (:gh:`6732`, :gh:`6735`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:284
msgid ""
"The ``from_settings()`` method of :class:`~scrapy.spidermiddlewares."
"urllength.UrlLengthMiddleware`, deprecated in Scrapy 2.12.0, is removed "
"earlier than the usual deprecation period (this was needed because after the "
"introduction of the :class:`~scrapy.spidermiddlewares.base."
"BaseSpiderMiddleware` base class and switching built-in spider middlewares "
"to it those middlewares need the :class:`~scrapy.crawler.Crawler` instance "
"at run time). Please use ``from_crawler()`` instead. (:gh:`6693`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:294
msgid ""
"``scrapy.utils.url.escape_ajax()`` is no longer called when a :class:"
"`~scrapy.Request` instance is created. It was only useful for websites "
"supporting the ``_escaped_fragment_`` feature which most modern websites "
"don't support. If you still need this you can modify the URLs before passing "
"them to :class:`~scrapy.Request`. (:gh:`6523`, :gh:`6651`)"
msgstr ""

