msgid ""
"It's deprecated to define an ``__init__()`` method that doesn't take a "
"``crawler`` argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:969
msgid ""
"It's deprecated to call an ``__init__()`` method without passing a "
"``crawler`` argument. If it's passed, it's also deprecated to pass a "
"``settings`` argument, which will be ignored anyway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:972
msgid ""
"Calling ``from_settings()`` is deprecated, use ``from_crawler()`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:974
msgid ""
"Overriding ``from_settings()`` is deprecated, override ``from_crawler()`` "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:979
msgid ""
"The ``REQUEST_FINGERPRINTER_IMPLEMENTATION`` setting is now deprecated. (:gh:"
"`6212`, :gh:`6213`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:982
msgid ""
"The ``scrapy.utils.misc.create_instance()`` function is now deprecated, use :"
"func:`scrapy.utils.misc.build_from_crawler` instead. (:gh:`5523`, :gh:"
"`5884`, :gh:`6162`, :gh:`6169`, :gh:`6540`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:986
msgid ""
"``scrapy.core.downloader.Downloader._get_slot_key()`` is deprecated, use :"
"meth:`scrapy.core.downloader.Downloader.get_slot_key` instead. (:gh:`6340`, :"
"gh:`6352`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:990
msgid ""
"``scrapy.utils.defer.process_chain_both()`` is now deprecated. (:gh:`6397`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:993
msgid ""
"``scrapy.twisted_version`` is now deprecated, you should instead use :attr:"
"`twisted.version` directly (but note that it's an ``incremental.Version`` "
"object, not a tuple). (:gh:`6509`, :gh:`6512`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:998
msgid ""
"``scrapy.utils.python.flatten()`` and ``scrapy.utils.python.iflatten()`` are "
"now deprecated. (:gh:`6517`, :gh:`6519`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1002
msgid ""
"``scrapy.utils.python.equal_attributes()`` is now deprecated. (:gh:`6517`, :"
"gh:`6519`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1005
msgid ""
"``scrapy.utils.request.request_authenticate()`` is now deprecated, you "
"should instead just set the ``Authorization`` header directly. (:gh:`6517`, :"
"gh:`6519`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1009
msgid ""
"``scrapy.utils.serialize.ScrapyJSONDecoder`` is now deprecated, it didn't "
"contain any code since Scrapy 1.0.0. (:gh:`6517`, :gh:`6519`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1013
msgid ""
"``scrapy.utils.test.assert_samelines()`` is now deprecated. (:gh:`6517`, :gh:"
"`6519`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1016
msgid ""
"``scrapy.extensions.feedexport.build_storage()`` is now deprecated. You can "
"instead call the builder callable directly. (:gh:`6540`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1020
msgid "``scrapy.utils.misc.md5sum()`` is now deprecated. (:gh:`6264`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1026
msgid ""
"``scrapy.Spider.start_requests()`` can now yield items. (:gh:`5289`, :gh:"
"`6417`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1029
msgid ""
"Some spider middlewares may need to be updated for Scrapy 2.12 support "
"before you can use them in combination with the ability to yield items from "
"``start_requests()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1033
msgid ""
"Added a new :class:`~scrapy.http.Response` subclass, :class:`~scrapy.http."
"JsonResponse`, for responses with a `JSON MIME type <https://mimesniff.spec."
"whatwg.org/#json-mime-type>`_. (:gh:`6069`, :gh:`6171`, :gh:`6174`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1038
msgid ""
"The :class:`~scrapy.extensions.logstats.LogStats` extension now adds "
"``items_per_minute`` and ``responses_per_minute`` to the :ref:`stats <topics-"
"stats>` when the spider closes. (:gh:`4110`, :gh:`4111`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1043
msgid ""
"Added :setting:`CLOSESPIDER_PAGECOUNT_NO_ITEM` which allows closing the "
"spider if no items were scraped in a set amount of time. (:gh:`6434`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/2.x.rst:1047
msgid "User-defined cookies can now include the ``secure`` field. (:gh:`6357`)"
msgstr ""

